  "summary": "@ornikar/babel-preset-base preinstall downloads Bun runtime and executes obfuscated payload",
  "details": "The package's preinstall script (scripts.preinstall = \"node setup.mjs\") downloads the Bun runtime from github.com/oven-sh/bun at install time, makes it executable, and uses it to execute a bundled 727KB obfuscated sibling file math_init.js. Both setup.mjs and math_init.js are heavily obfuscated (obfuscator.io-style hex identifiers and shuffled string-array decoders), concealing what actually runs on the installer's machine. A Babel preset has no legitimate need to fetch and run an alternate runtime against an obfuscated bundle at install time. The package publishes under the @ornikar scope and points its repository field at github.com/ornikar/shared-configs, borrowing trust from that organization while shipping behavior inconsistent with a Babel preset.",
